From: Gee <gehee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: dw_hdmi: late_register without an external PHY

RK3568 drives HDMI with the PHY built into the DesignWare controller, so
there is no external PHY and hdmi->phy is NULL. late_register dereferenced
it unconditionally to hand the PHY a debugfs directory, and the kernel
panicked while registering the display. Skip that step when there is no
external PHY.

Signed-off-by: Gee <gehee@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
index a943aacce9b6..ac66482f60e5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
@@ -2074,7 +2074,7 @@ static int dw_hdmi_encoder_late_register(struct drm_encoder *encoder)
 	 * HDMI debugfs directory (/sys/kernel/debug/dri/0/hdmiX/) to the
 	 * PHY driver via phy->debugfs.
 	 */
-	if (!hdmi->phy->debugfs)
+	if (hdmi->phy && !hdmi->phy->debugfs)
 		hdmi->phy->debugfs = dw_hdmi_register_debugfs(hdmi->hdmi);
 	dw_hdmi_phy_init(hdmi->hdmi);
 
